  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1116 AM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nTowards the middle/end of the week the upper low opens into an\nopen wave that merges with a longwave trough axis approaching the\nOhio Valley region. This should continue to lower shower and\nthunderstorm chances into the low to medium chance category. \n\nGFS shows a convective complex developing over the southeast.\nHowever, this looks alot like convective feedback at this time. So\nstaying with lower pop Thursday into Friday (20-40%). However, \nwill need to monitor this period for high precipitation chance \npotential if that materializes. An overall increase in high \ntemperatures are expected Wednesday through the end of next week. \nHighs should rebound back into the upper 80s to lower 90s in most \nlocations with more sunshine in the morning expected. \n\nModels do seem a bit more convergent on a weak front (longwave\ntrough axis aloft) push east into the Tennessee Valley into the\nweekend. This could kept low to medium chances of showers and\nthunderstorms in the forecast next weekend. Again, shear and\ninstability looks to weak for stronger thunderstorm concerns.\nDangerous heat index values over 100 degrees may build back into\nthe region next weekend.",
